  {
    "str": "A B S T R A C T",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.3547145587570131,
      "width": 0.09076754218379382,
      "height": 0.008786306178271162
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "The fracture behaviour of (Hf-Ta-Zr-Nb)C high-entropy carbide grains was investigated by microcantilever",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.37974879709109605,
      "width": 0.5955721863471737,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "bending experiments, and fracture related properties (e.g. strength, toughness) were determined using linear",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.39182006334879255,
      "width": 0.5955673663981077,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "beam theory. Microcantilevers were FIB-milled from large grains with {001} and {101} orientations and were",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.4038913296064891,
      "width": 0.5955673663981079,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "subjected to micro-bending experiments. SEM based fractographic analysis of the broken cantilevers revealed",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.4159625958641856,
      "width": 0.5955866461943706,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "that approximately half of them fractured at the fixing position at FIB-induced surface cracks, while the rest of",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.42796246659636306,
      "width": 0.5955239868565174,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "the beams failed at small cracks located at submicron size pores or inclusions. In all cases, fracture occurred on",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.4400337328540596,
      "width": 0.595570981359907,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "the {001} cleavage plane. The fracture strength of beams fractured at the fixing position was 11.8 ± 0.2 GPa,",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.4521049991117561,
      "width": 0.5956143609014981,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "while the strength of the beams that failed at submicron defects was in the range of 3.8-8.9 GPa. The calculation",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.46410486984393357,
      "width": 0.5955926711307026,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "of stress concentration in the vicinity of pores revealed that local stress field exceeded the value that induced",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.4761761361016301,
      "width": 0.5955878511816374,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "cracking in ‘defect free’ beams.",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.34123834994187574,
      "top": 0.4882474023593266,
      "width": 0.16770771776453275,
      "height": 0.00903740829355135
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "1. Introduction",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.5426009290652274,
      "width": 0.09949838585798858,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "High-entropy ultra-high temperature ceramics are a novel group of",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.08409378587411555,
      "top": 0.5689573548099347,
      "width": 0.4007878100746545,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "materials, which are being developed to broaden the limited set of",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.582099919680081,
      "width": 0.42173878488297867,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "ultra-high temperature ceramics (UHTCs), comprising about 15 mate-",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.5953137805546421,
      "width": 0.4217789516291602,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "rials [1], and improve their mechanical properties to meet the con-",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.6084573495938647,
      "width": 0.4217749349545421,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "tinuously",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.6216712104684258,
      "width": 0.05512216467655341,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "growing",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.12666518126045734,
      "top": 0.6216712104684258,
      "width": 0.04870887420289076,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "demands",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.1838077332699454,
      "top": 0.6216712104684258,
      "width": 0.05277910448262655,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "of",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.24494955430758175,
      "top": 0.6216712104684258,
      "width": 0.011648356392664918,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "ultra-high",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.2649499161229414,
      "top": 0.6216712104684258,
      "width": 0.0589380055638057,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "temperature",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.3322827716387022,
      "top": 0.6216712104684258,
      "width": 0.07255453251936918,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "applications",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.4132334930015658,
      "top": 0.6216712104684258,
      "width": 0.07168425301876777,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "[2,3]. In general, UTHCs are defined as materials with melting tem-",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.6348137753385721,
      "width": 0.4218204572668815,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "perature above 3000 °C that can withstand extreme environments for",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.6480276362131332,
      "width": 0.4217361070998999,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "applications above 1500 °C in oxidizing and aggressive environments,",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.6611712052523556,
      "width": 0.421799035002251,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "such as rocket propulsions, hypersonic and re-usable atmospheric re-",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.6743850661269168,
      "width": 0.42178966276147534,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "entry vehicles. UHTCs are usually based on the refractory borides,",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.687527630997063,
      "width": 0.4217628849306876,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "carbides and nitrides of the group of IV and V transition metals. Due to",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.7007414918716242,
      "width": 0.42183116839919627,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "the nature of their chemical bonds, these materials exhibit high hard-",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.7138840567417705,
      "width": 0.4217575293645301,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "ness (>20 GPa) and strength (>500 MPa) with excellent oxidation and",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.7270989217854079,
      "width": 0.4217628849306878,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "ablation resistance at elevated temperatures [4–6].",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.7402414866555541,
      "width": 0.3048428423621983,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "Based on the discovery of high-entropy alloys [7,8] and entropy-",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.08409378587411555,
      "top": 0.7534553475301153,
      "width": 0.4008467213023875,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "stabilized oxides [9], bulk high-entropy UHTCs have been successfully",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.7665979124002615,
      "width": 0.4217669016053059,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "synthesized both from metal diborides by Gild el al. [2] and from metal",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.779812777443899,
      "width": 0.4217561904729908,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "carbides by the present authors [3]. These novel high-entropy ceramics",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.7929553423140452,
      "width": 0.42175619047299073,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "are composed of four or more different transition metal elements of",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.8061692031886063,
      "width": 0.4217387848829786,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "equimolar proportions and boron or carbon atoms, and form hexagonal",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.06314281106579134,
      "top": 0.8193830640631674,
      "width": 0.42181911837534203,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "or cubic solid solution structures, respectively. Experimental and the-",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.5150428056565359,
      "top": 0.5426009290652274,
      "width": 0.42174547934067547,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "oretical studies on these materials suggest that high-entropy ultra-high",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.5150428056565359,
      "top": 0.5557434939353737,
      "width": 0.42179100165301475,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "temperature ceramics could broaden the limited set of UHTCs and their",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.5150428056565359,
      "top": 0.5689573548099347,
      "width": 0.42170531259449406,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "mechanical properties could go beyond those of the base borides [2]",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "left": 0.5150428056565359,
      "top": 0.582099919680081,
      "width": 0.4217173626183485,
      "height": 0.010041690762642356
    }
  },
  {
    "str": "and carbides [3,10–13]. Regarding high-entropy carbides, Castle et al.",
    "box": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
